      "content": "thanks. that's a good start. i want to make it even more aggressive though. they've been ignoring my family for decades, so i need to hint that i know something about the \"off-book\" side of these contracts. basically, i want to mention that the grandfather's agreements include clauses that bypass the current management and go straight to the primary shareholders if certain conditions aren't met. can you help me phrase that in a way that sounds legally intimidating and makes it clear that i have the leverage to disrupt their current control?",
